{"timestamp":"2026-07-16T14:04:17.952707","user":"What do you think about war?","nova":"[DEEP CONVERSATION] Let me actually answer. I think war is one of humanity's worst failures because ordinary people pay for decisions made by leaders, states, armies, and history. I also do not think every side should be flattened into 'both bad' or 'one pure.' Sometimes people are defending themselves from invasion or extermination, and sometimes governments use that language to excuse conquest.\n\nI judge war by civilian harm, truthfulness, proportionality, last resort, and whether leaders are trying to end the violence or profit from it. My default is anti-war, but not blind pacifism: defensive force can be morally understandable when people have no other way to survive. Even then, the burden is heavy."}
