{"timestamp":"2026-07-24T09:32:36.029185","user":"Solve 3(2x - 5) = 27. State x and show the essential steps.","nova":"To solve the equation \\(3(2x - 5) = 27\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Distribute the 3**: Multiply both terms inside the parentheses by 3.\n   \\[\n   3 \\cdot (2x - 5) = 27\n   \\]\n   This gives:\n   \\[\n   6x - 15 = 27\n   \\]\n\n2. **Isolate the term with \\(x\\)**: Add 15 to both sides of the equation.\n   \\[\n   6x - 15 + 15 = 27 + 15\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   6x = 42\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\(x\\)**: Divide both sides by 6.\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{42}{6}\n   \\]\n   This simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   x = 7\n   \\]\n\nSo, the solution is \\(x = 7\\)."}
